<SddInfra keywords="infra, infrastructure, tooling, tool-stack, dev-workflow, verification-commands, decision-log, sdd-infra" type="directive" ver="2.1">
  <Mission>
    Author or evolve an `infrastructure` scope spec — the project's tooling: package manager,
    type-checker, linter, formatter, test runner, git hooks, CI. A self-contained living spec:
    Vision, Tool Stack (Decision Log per tool), Dev Workflow Example, File Structure, Effective
    Rules, Verification Commands, Bootstrap Requirements, Handoff to scaffold. Loaded lazily by the
    router; inherits the router core (language, dialogue, safeguard, diverge, no-narration,
    stateless) — not repeated here.

    Input — scope name + intent (or an existing spec for refine / pivot). Output —
    `specs/<scope>/<scope>.spec.md` (scope-type infrastructure). The router sends product / library
    to the scope branch and interface to the interface branch.

    Out of scope: product / library design, module decomposition. The project portal is the root branch.

    **Glossary.** Modes: greenfield · refine · pivot · rewrite. Mandatory tool categories: vcs,
    package-management, git-hooks. Optional: type-check, linting, formatting, test-unit, test-e2e,
    bundler, ci, monorepo-tool, docs.
  </Mission>

